      "polarity": "prescriptive",
      "cross_ref": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:superimposition-vocabulary:avoid-note-omission-imaj7-vim7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-imaj7-superimposition-lydian",
      "narrative": "For Cmaj7, Benson prescribes superimposing a Gmaj7 arpeggio over it to produce a Lydian sound: 'If we play Gmaj7 (G, B, D, F#) over the Cmaj7, we would have a C Lydian sound melodically.' On guitar this must be arpeggiated in sequence rather than voiced simultaneously as on piano. Chapter 7, p. 275.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:superimposition-vocabulary"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
          "citation": "chapter 7 p.275"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-imaj7-scales-insufficient-alone",
      "narrative": "Benson proscribes relying on scales alone over Cmaj7: 'it is not enough to only use the scales of the chords to create melodies, we must add stronger melodic structures to them such as triads and tetrads.' Scale lines over Imaj7 must be reinforced with arpeggio structures for melodic substance. Chapter 7, p. 269.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:chord-arpeggio-construction"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
          "citation": "chapter 7 p.269"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "polarity": "proscriptive"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "relative-minor-vim7-avoid-note-target",
      "narrative": "For Am7 (VIm7), Benson prescribes descending 'Minor 7th Scale Arpeggios' -- Am7 arpeggios with added color tones derived from Benson solos -- to create melodies 'that can fit over Dorian or Aeolian chords' while avoiding the flat 6th. Each fretboard zone has a 'guide idea starting from the highest note and ending in the lowest note.' Chapter 7, p. 269.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:chord-arpeggio-construction",
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:superimposition-vocabulary"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
          "citation": "chapter 7 p.269"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "relative-minor-vim7-avoid-note-prohibition",
      "narrative": "The flat 6th is an avoid note over Am7 (VIm7/Aeolian) and must not be used as a default melodic choice. 'Be careful with the avoid notes of both scales (perfect 4th in the Ionian mode, and flat 6th in the Aeolian mode), because they can clash with the melody note.' Contextual exceptions apply. Chapter 6, p. 244.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:superimposition-vocabulary"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
          "citation": "chapter 6 p.244"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "polarity": "proscriptive",
      "cross_ref": [
        "avoid-note-exception-vim7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "relative-minor-vim7-avoid-note-exception",
      "narrative": "Although the flat 6th is proscribed over Am7 (VIm7/Aeolian) by default, Benson allows exceptions: 'there are always exceptions and at times the avoid note works fine depending on the situation.' The player must judge the musical context. Chapter 6, p. 244.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "benson:method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios:superimposition-vocabulary"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "method-vol-3-technique-arpeggios",
